; Host - which target this compiler binary itself runs on.
; See `Host.darwin-aarch64.ax` for why this is a compile-time constant
; selected by module resolution rather than a runtime query.
;
; This file exists so that compiling the compiler FOR windows-x86_64
; resolves `Host` at all - the alternative is `cannot read module:
; Host`, which is the loud failure that module's comment asks for.
; No compiler binary has yet run on Windows: hosting the compiler
; there is a later phase of the Windows track, after the executing CI
; leg and the file-I/O half of `Sys/Platform.windows.ax`.
(pub :: hostTarget String)

(pub fn (hostTarget) "windows-x86_64")
